      {
        "id": 214560,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-15T18:47:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>@MindWanderer and Powerhound:&nbsp; I grok your arguments, and I don't disagree.&nbsp; But are we really supposed to be playing \"80s-vigilante/murderer/borderline-villain\" Parse?&nbsp; I don't think it's an accident that we first get to play her in Vengeance: the first real event in which she actively works *with* heroes and has her proverbial \"Come to Jeebus\" moment of \"Man...maybe I'm not as infallible as I thought I was.\"&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Not saying that the base arrow-shot is a-thematic; just that a power that might demonstrate her targeting of weak points might provide something that's more in line with her role as a hero, rather than as a murderous loner.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:47.572Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
