      {
        "id": 214563,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-16T14:58:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"PlatinumWarlock\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/48/1869_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> PlatinumWarlock:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Trajector wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>Yeah, I'm kind of curious as to why Parse's base power is straight-up \"deal 2 damage\" instead of something like, maybe, \"Parse deals 1 target 1 damage, increase the next damage dealt to that target by 1.\" That would have (90% of the time) the same effect on the total damage dealt, but would fit a little better thematically.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>Agreed; that’d be more thematic and definitely push her farther away from the archer-stereotype, though it might slightly take away from Targeting Arrow.  With that said, I wouldn’t have an issue with making the effective text on Targeting Arrow into her base power, then replacing it with a card capable of scanning/manipulating other hero decks.  Perhaps something like, “Reveal the top 3 cards of each Hero’s deck.  Place those cards back on top of their relevant decks in any order you choose.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I mean, I’d change the power but leave Targeting Arrow alone - that way, she has several ways to “mark” targets and could even do it multiple times per turn. That seems like it fits the way the character uses her arrows while still allowing her to be murder-y.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:47.847Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
