      {
        "id": 214564,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-19T20:03:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Phantom5613 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Well, one thing I definitly took away from all this is that I've been thinking about Parse's deck&nbsp;totally wrong. I should have been thinking about her as a 'super-computer analyzer' style character opposed to a 'trick\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nYeah, I'm kind of curious as to why Parse's base power is straight-up \"deal 2 damage\" instead of something like, maybe, \"Parse deals 1 target 1 damage, increase the next damage dealt to that target by 1.\" That would have (90% of the time) the same effect on the total damage dealt, but would fit a little better thematically.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wait, you never use Parse to kill targets with 2 hp left?&nbsp; Changing the power this way would kill a <span class=\"bbcode-i\">huge</span> amount of utility.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:47.937Z",
