        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-20T03:41:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Trajector wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote> Phantom5613 wrote:<br>\n<blockquote>Well, one thing I definitly took away from all this is that I've been thinking about Parse's deck totally wrong. I should have been thinking about her as a 'super-computer analyzer' style character opposed to a 'trick \n</blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, I’m kind of curious as to why Parse’s base power is straight-up “deal 2 damage” instead of something like, maybe, “Parse deals 1 target 1 damage, increase the next damage dealt to that target by 1.” That would have (90% of the time) the same effect on the total damage dealt, but would fit a little better thematically.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>Wait, you never use Parse to kill targets with 2 hp left?  Changing the power this way would kill a  huge  amount of utility.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well, sure I do, but that’s my point: she’s not supposed to be the trick archer character, as we’ve just learned.</p>",
